- Write the one-pass "seen-so-far" complement lookup without the self-pair bug, and explain precisely why the query must come before the insert.
- Turn any "when do two objects match?" rule into a **key** — $a_i - i$, $a_i \bmod k$, a sorted tuple — and count groups with a single `Counter` pass.
- Prove and implement Boyer–Moore voting in $O(1)$ memory, for majorities above $n/2$ and above $n/3$, including the verification pass that makes the $n/3$ version honest.
